WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.778
The second extension asks whether many models are better than one.

00:00:04.228 --> 00:00:06.082
We built three kinds of branches.

00:00:06.532 --> 00:00:12.101
One models returns with raw, DWT or MODWT ARMA GARCH.

00:00:12.551 --> 00:00:15.396
One fits an ARMA directly to the past targets.

00:00:15.846 --> 00:00:24.187
And one decomposes the target itself into scales, a smooth part plus details, forecasts each component, and adds them back up.

00:00:24.637 --> 00:00:28.541
Then an ensemble simply averages the forecasts with equal weights.

00:00:28.991 --> 00:00:29.644
Did it help?

00:00:30.094 --> 00:00:32.762
For Tunisia, Nigeria and Infosys.

00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:38.846
For Nigeria the combined ensemble cuts MSE by about 6 percent compared with raw GARCH.

00:00:39.296 --> 00:00:43.720
For the other series the ensembles are worse, by 1 to 22 percent.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:44.662
Why?

00:00:45.112 --> 00:00:48.477
Look at the average forecast divided by the average target.

00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:52.527
Raw GARCH overshoots a little, by 6 to 37 percent.

00:00:52.977 --> 00:00:58.191
The DWT model's ratio ranges from 1.00 to 1.48.

00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:02.387
Averaging weaker members dilutes the best model instead of improving it.
